-- The Courts Law's own references into this Basic Law (to s 4, s 4(a), s 4(d), s 4(f), s 7(4)) are in row IL-38.

GIVEN ref IS A `A cross-reference`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the cross-reference agrees` MEANS
    ref's `what the citing text says it points at` EQUALS ref's `what the cited provision deals with`

GIVEN refs IS A LIST OF `A cross-reference`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`every cross-reference in the list agrees` MEANS
    CONSIDER refs
    WHEN EMPTY THEN TRUE
    WHEN r FOLLOWED BY rest THEN `the cross-reference agrees` r AND `every cross-reference in the list agrees` rest

`the cross-references of sections 4A, 4B and 4(e), (f)` MEANS
    LIST `xref 4A(a)(1) to 4(e)`,
         `xref 4A(b)(1) to 4(d)(2)`,
         `xref 4A(b)(2) to 4(d)(3)`,
         `xref 4A(c) to 4(a)`,
         `xref 4A(d)(2) to 4(a)`,
         `xref 4B to 4(b)(1)(b)-(d)`,
         `xref 4(e) to 4(d)`,
         `xref 4(f)(2) to 4(b)(1)(d)`,
         `xref 4(f)(3) to 4(d)`,
         `xref 4(f)(3) to 4(e)`,
         `xref 4(f)(3) to 4(d)(3)`,
         `xref 4B(1) to Basic Law The Knesset s 9`,
         `xref 4B(2) to Basic Law The Knesset s 34`,
         `xref 4B(2) to Basic Law The Knesset s 36A`,
         `xref 4B(2) to Basic Law The Government s 11(b)`,
         `xref 4B(2) to Basic Law The Government s 29(f)`,
         `xref 4B(3) to Basic Law The Government s 18`,
         `xref 4B(3) to Basic Law The Government s 19`,
         `xref 4B(3) to Basic Law The Government s 20`,
         `xref 4B(3) to Basic Law The Government s 21`,
         `xref 4B(3) to Basic Law The Government s 29(a)`,
         `xref 4B(4) to Basic Law The Government s 28`
